1
00:00:00,000 --> 00:00:05,304
Narrator: Scenario 13. Infrastructure operations.

2
00:00:05,904 --> 00:00:15,432
A: The log volume is ninety-two percent full. Based on the last thirty minutes of growth, it may reach capacity within about two hours.

3
00:00:16,032 --> 00:00:25,512
B: Can we delete the oldest files now? I would like to create breathing room before the volume fills and the application starts failing writes.

4
00:00:26,112 --> 00:00:37,776
A: I will check the retention policy and archive status first. Some older logs support an active investigation, so age alone does not establish deletion eligibility.

5
00:00:38,376 --> 00:00:48,888
B: Understood. What is driving the growth? If rotation stopped working, a one-time cleanup could give us only a short period of relief.

6
00:00:49,488 --> 00:01:00,096
A: The current log file is growing unusually fast, and yesterday’s rotation task failed. I am checking permissions and the task error before changing anything.

7
00:01:00,696 --> 00:01:11,544
B: Please also check whether debug logging was enabled during troubleshooting. We should ask the application owner before reducing anything needed for the investigation.

8
00:01:12,144 --> 00:01:22,392
A: The owner confirmed extra debug logging can end now under the troubleshooting plan. I will restore the normal level and preserve the relevant evidence.

9
00:01:22,992 --> 00:01:32,520
B: How much space can approved cleanup recover, and do we need expansion as well? Please account for the time required to grow the filesystem.

10
00:01:33,120 --> 00:01:44,208
A: Verified archived files should release about fifteen percent of the volume. I am also checking online expansion support and available storage with the platform owner.

11
00:01:44,808 --> 00:01:55,944
B: Use the approved cleanup procedure and avoid truncating files that are still open. If expansion is needed, submit the appropriate change with the capacity evidence.

12
00:01:56,544 --> 00:02:07,776
A: I will report usage and the new growth rate by 13:00 UTC. After repairing rotation, I will verify the next cycle rather than assume it works.

13
00:02:08,376 --> 00:02:20,160
B: I will review the expansion recommendation at that checkpoint. Keep the application owner informed and verify normal log writes before closing the immediate capacity risk.
